music marks, source selection, structural parent and g a share one target
real configured model returns BL that passes browser compilation and graph validation
refinement retains versions; selecting an older candidate never changes source or playback
an intervening performance edit disables commit until the candidate is auditioned again
candidate audition produces a measured non-silent signal on its separate monitor bus
audition preserves active history; commit updates the draft and activates at a future bar
undo restores source and the previous performance through the same revision scheduler
invalid generated music leaves source and the active performance unchanged
cancel returns control immediately and drops the request-owned candidate
narrow layout preserves the real source pane and reachable phrase controls
real unuse closes audio/graphics and removes the workspace while preserving source and cursor
